  "result": "I fixed the bug and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/pricing.py:10`, `line_subtotal` checked `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD` with `BULK_THRESHOLD = 10`. Using \"greater than\" means the discount only started at 11 units. That doesn't match the policy of \"10 or more\".\n\n**Fix:** I changed the check to `line.qty >= BULK_THRESHOLD`. Tax is worked out from the same function, so the discounted amount now also feeds into `calc_total` and `calc_tax`.\n\nThe existing test `test_bulk_discount` already expected this. It buys 10 units at $1.00 and expects $10.28: $10.00, minus the 5% discount is $9.50, plus 8.25% tax is $10.28. The test file passes cleanly now. I didn't run the suite before the change, so I haven't confirmed that this test was failing.",
